WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.067
-Willem Dafoe, they love you.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.534
Thanks for coming back
on the show.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:04.968
-Yeah, my pleasure.
-You look good.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.400
What is the look?
-I don't look good.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.734
-No, you do look good.
-This is for a movie.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:09.901
It's not for life.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.901
[ Laughter ]
I look in the mirror

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:14.467
and I see Joe Stalin.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.267
[ Laughter ]
-No!
-Yeah.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.267
When I look to the side,

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.968
I see a '70s biker.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.367
[ Laughter ]
-But that's not what it's for.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.367
-You've never grown facial hair
just for fun?

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.434
-No, I have, but, you know,
it's kind of a drag.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:30.467
When I was younger,
when you grew hair

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.367
for a role,
it was something special.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.334
Now, it's in vogue, you know...
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.901
-...and it's almost cooler
to be cleanshaven.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:40.100
-Oh, thank you very much.
I appreciate that. Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.601
[ Laughter ]
That's why I do it.
-I don't go for the beard

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.200
on you.
-Yeah. You didn't go for it?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.534
-No, no, no, no.
-I tried to do the beard.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.834
I just figured I never tried it.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.934
I never actually tried it
and really meant to try it.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.634
-It looked good,
but it ain't you.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.334
[ Laughter ]
-Ah. Thank you, buddy.
I appreciate that.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.501
Thank you very much.
I like that.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.300
I tried it and it wasn't me.
Yeah.
-No.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.067
-No. This is more me, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.701
-But you can be a chameleon.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.367
You can do this.
You can do that.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.033
You're always different
in all the looks.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.968
But you're always looking good
because you're a movie star.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:07.133
-Thank you.
-Last time we were on the show,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.968
we talked about "Spider-Man"
and now, it's made over,

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:13.133
you know, $150 billion,
something crazy-amazing.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.067
But we all love you
as Green Goblin.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.801
-Great.
-Fan favorite.
Everyone loves you.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.501
-Great. Yeah.
Yeah, of course.

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:22.434
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.501
But --
-But...

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.567
-But there is a thing going
around online

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.467
that I was looking at
that everyone wants you

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:32.000
to play a different --
They want you to play Joker.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.634
[ Oohs ]
-Hasn't that been done?

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.400
-No, but, but I mean, but --

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.801
-You know, talk to Warner Bros.

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.767
[ Laughter ]
-Really? I'll talk
to Warner Bros.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.133
Are you guys watching?
Yeah. Hello.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:45.000
-I floated an idea a while ago,
but it didn't quite happen, so.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.734
-What was the idea?
Can you say it, or no?

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.767
-Ah... You know, I --
-You can't?

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.434
-Listen, I didn't really
float it to them.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.968
I just mentioned it
in an interview

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:55.067
and then it kind of went
out on the Internet.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:59.767
But I thought it would be cool
for me to play an impostor,

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.100
like slipstreaming his thing.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.801
-Oh, yeah, like,
"I'm the new Joker. I'm Joker."

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:08.133
Yeah. And Joaquin could be like,
"Oh, yeah?"

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.267
I love this!
-It would be cool.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.801
-Yes, you could do that!
-But we're doing --

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.634
[ Cheering and applause ]
we're doing --

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.367
we're doing other things.
-Yeah, you're doing

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:17.667
other things.
Things are going okay.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.267
Yeah. You know,
it's award season now

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:23.000
and I know you've been nominated
for how many Oscars, now?

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.601
-Four.
-Yeah. No big deal. Yeah.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:28.701
[ Whistling ]

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.467
Do you remember the first time

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:31.567
you got nominated for an Oscar?

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.434
-The first time
I remember really well

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.901
because it wasn't as developed,

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:38.767
you know, the campaigning
and all that sort of thing

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.067
and my son's babysitter
called me up

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.467
to tell me I was nominated.

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:43.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.334
I mean, and by the time --

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.067
the second time, you know,

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.634
you could barely
sleep the night before

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.501
because you were aware that
the nominations were coming out.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:54.100
So, it's become
much more developed.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.167
-What was it for, "Platoon"?
Was that the first one?

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.067
-First one was "Platoon."

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:01.801
Second one was for something
called "Shadow of the Vampire."

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:04.968
Third was for "Florida Project"

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.334
and fourth was
for "At Eternity's Gate."

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.801
-And do you get nervous
when you --

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:10.901
Because now you're nominated
and you go, "Okay,"

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:12.501
and you go like, "[ Exhales
forcefully ] I got a shot.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.267
I can, you know."
And is it fun?

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:15.868
-You know, it becomes a game

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.167
and you do, you know,
you do your best

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.267
to throw your hat in the ring
and try to win.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.133
If you're competitive,
it's kind of fun.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:26.868
But, you know, it's --
I'll say it, I'll say it.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.100
You're going to hear it.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.934
It's nice to be nominated.
-There you go.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.601
[ Cheering and applause ]
You actually said it.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:32.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.501
He actually said it.
Good!

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.601
But I think it must be fun.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.901
-But that's not happening
this year, so let's --

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:42.501
-Next year.
Next year, it's happening.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.601
I want to talk
about your new movie, "Inside."

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:48.467
It's a psychological drama
and it's pretty much you

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.601
on the screen
for two hours, almost,

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.267
and you're fantastic in it.
You're getting great reviews.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:54.567
I don't know if you want
to hear them...

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.567
-Alright, go ahead.
-...but I'm going to say them.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.567
[ Laughter ]
-I'll go like this.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.000
-Yeah, perfect.
Deadline says,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.934
"Willem Dafoe delivers
a tour de force performance."

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
Tour de force. Ooh, French!

00:04:05.534 --> 00:04:07.434
-Oui oui.
-Collider says,

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.701
"Everything is glued together

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.934
by another Dafoe performance
that proves he's one

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.300
of the greatest actors
of all time."

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.534
[ Cheering and applause ]
Not too shabby! Come on!

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.033
-Thank you very much!

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.634
Thank you.
-That is not too shabby.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.300
Oh, yeah, I have this here.
How --

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.067
Yeah, I found these.
I forgot I had them.

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:26.868
[ Laughter ]
-You --

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.901
-Here you go.
Yeah.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.334
How --

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:33.367
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:35.567
I feel I could play your --
-Yeah.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:36.734
-I could play your brother.
-Yeah.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:37.934
I can play your brother
in the movie.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:38.934
-Yeah!
-Right?

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:41.634
Come on down.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.133
We'll go work on it together.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:44.801
Can we set up the premise
of this movie?

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.234
-Sure, yeah.
This premise is great

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:49.767
and it's really simple.
For once.

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:51.968
[ Laughter ]
You know, I play an art thief

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:57.067
that is breaking
into a penthouse in New York.

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:59.901
This place has a lot
of priceless art

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.133
and I hack
into the security system.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:06.200
I go to take three
Egon Schiele paintings.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.734
I go there, I get in,
I'm ready to go, I hack out,

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:13.434
and the system goes awry
and closes me in.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:16.234
-Yeah, the alarms go off.
-And nobody comes.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.067
I'm stuck there.
The cops don't come.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:20.267
The owner doesn't come.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.334
All the smart systems
in the house

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.834
of this real high-tech house
go wacky

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.334
and I got to survive there

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.534
and I don't know when
I'm ever going to get out.

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:30.267
And the guy hasn't been there
for a while,

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.767
so, I got to deal with food.
I got to deal with water.

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.734
And then, with time,

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:37.968
I start to deal with the art
and deal with being there.

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:41.000
And it's interesting
because there's a very strong

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.968
narrative plotline

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.701
of he's got to deal
with these things

00:05:44.701 --> 00:05:46.734
and you kind of figure it out
with him.

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.100
But at the same time,

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.100
there's lots of interesting
things that are raised

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.567
about our relationship
to art and luxury

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:55.434
and what we need
and what's important.

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:58.901
So, it's pretty cool
because it works on,

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:01.501
at least, two levels.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:03.601
[ Laughter ]
I will say, when I was watching,
I would go,

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.400
"What would I do
if I was in that position?"

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.000
-Well, yeah,
that's what happens.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.300
-And everyone bails on you,

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.968
everyone who planned it out,
and you go --

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:11.100
-Well, you got to deal
-You're by yourself.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.501
-with yourself, you know?

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:13.767
you got to deal with yourself

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.501
and you got to figure out
what you need, that's all.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:17.801
-You guys got to watch this.
It's great.

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:20.968
I want to show a clip.
Here's Willem Dafoe in "Inside."

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:21.701
Take a look at this.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.601
-Go to Tompkins Square Park.

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:32.567
Look for a guy named Danny Z.

00:06:32.567 --> 00:06:36.067
He's usually near
the basketball courts.

00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:38.033
[Indistinct]

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:43.400
Tell him that I'm stuck here.

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:46.667
No one's come.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.868
-[ Warbling ]

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:50.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:59.501
[ Wind whipping ]
[ Tap ]

00:06:59.501 --> 00:07:00.234
[ Tap ]

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.767
[ Tapping ]
Do that for me.

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:07.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Whoa!

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.033
Come on!

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:09.067
Whoo!

00:07:09.067 --> 00:07:11.033
Willem Dafoe, everybody!

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:14.667
Go see "Inside,"
in theaters March 17th.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.701
Marlon Wayans joins us
after the break.

00:07:16.701 --> 00:07:17.601
Stick around, everybody.

